3. INSTALLATION TELEMETRY, DATA PROTECTION & CALIFORNIA/US PRIVACY
To enforce domain licensing, deliver compatibility checks, and track active
installations, the Cloud DRM Client edition transmits minimal, non-personal
installation telemetry to RouteRequestServer upon module installation,
activation, version change, and periodic heartbeats (at most once every 24
hours). Transmitted data is strictly limited to:
  - Installation web address / domain (app.url) and VA site name;
  - Installed RouteRequest version, build edition, and PHP version;
  - License activation state (activated vs. unactivated) and key prefix.
No pilot personal data (pilot names, emails, IP addresses, or PIREPs) is
collected by telemetry. Full details on how current and future data are stored,
encrypted, retained, and protected under California (CalOPPA, CCPA/CPRA) and
United States laws are set forth in PRIVACY.md. Telemetry operates in fail-open
mode so brief outages do not disrupt your VA, though an internet connection is
required for license activation, Cloud DRM features, and updates.

